BT /F2 13 Tf 54 620.0 Td (1. Purpose and Scope) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 597.0 Td (This document defines the AI Management System \(AIMS\) established by Hewlett Packard Enterprise to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 583.0 Td (govern the responsible design, development, deployment, and operation of artificial intelligence) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 569.0 Td (across the enterprise, in conformance with ISO/IEC 42001:2023. The scope of the AIMS covers three) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 555.0 Td (flagship AI capabilities: GreenLake AIOps \(autonomous infrastructure optimization and anomaly) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 541.0 Td (detection\), Aruba AI \(network assurance, client fingerprinting, and edge inference\), and HPEFS fraud) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 527.0 Td (models \(Hewlett Packard Enterprise Financial Services credit and transaction fraud scoring\). The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 513.0 Td (AIMS applies to all HPE personnel, contractors, and third-party model providers whose systems fall) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 499.0 Td (within these product boundaries, including the data pipelines, MLOps platforms, and cloud regions) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 485.0 Td (that support them.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 465.0 Td (Interested parties considered in defining scope include customers, regulators, data subjects,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 451.0 Td (channel partners, and internal engineering and risk functions. External and internal issues) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 437.0 Td (affecting the AIMS - evolving AI regulation, model supply-chain dependencies, and customer trust) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 423.0 Td (expectations - are reviewed at least annually.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 397.0 Td (2. AI Policy and Objectives) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 374.0 Td (HPE maintains an AI Policy, approved by top management, that commits the organization to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 360.0 Td (trustworthy, lawful, transparent, and human-centric AI. The policy establishes principles of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 346.0 Td (fairness, accountability, safety, security, privacy, and explainability, and requires that all) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 332.0 Td (in-scope AI systems undergo impact and risk evaluation before release.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 312.0 Td (Measurable AI objectives derived from the policy include: maintaining false-positive rates below) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 298.0 Td (defined thresholds for HPEFS fraud models; achieving documented AI impact assessment coverage of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 284.0 Td (100% for high-consequence systems; sustaining model-drift detection within agreed tolerances for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 270.0 Td (GreenLake AIOps; and closing all critical nonconformities within 30 days. Objectives are tracked) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 256.0 Td (quarterly and reported to the AI Governance Board.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 230.0 Td (3. Leadership and Commitment) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 207.0 Td (Top management commitment is demonstrated through the AI Governance Board, chaired by the Chief AI &) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 193.0 Td (Data Governance Officer and including representatives from Legal, Security, Privacy, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 179.0 Td (business-unit engineering leadership. Leadership ensures the AI Policy and objectives are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 165.0 Td (established, compatible with HPE's strategic direction, and integrated into business processes.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 151.0 Td (Management allocates the resources - funding, tooling, platform capacity, and qualified personnel -) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 137.0 Td (necessary to operate and continually improve the AIMS. Roles, responsibilities, and authorities for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 123.0 Td (AI governance are formally assigned, including a designated AIMS owner and accountable system owners) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 109.0 Td (for each product.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 83.0 Td (4. Planning: Risk, Opportunities and Controls) Tj ET
