BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738.0 Td (The AIMS follows a risk-based planning approach. HPE identifies risks and opportunities that could) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 724.0 Td (affect the AIMS achieving its intended outcomes, addressing both organizational risk and risk to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 710.0 Td (individuals and society. For each in-scope system, a formal risk assessment evaluates likelihood and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 696.0 Td (severity of potential harms, and an AI impact assessment \(AIIA\) examines consequences to affected) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 682.0 Td (persons - for example, wrongful fraud declines by HPEFS models, network access errors from Aruba AI,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 668.0 Td (or operational disruption from GreenLake AIOps automation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 648.0 Td (Identified risks drive selection of controls from Annex A of ISO/IEC 42001, documented in a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 634.0 Td (Statement of Applicability. Controls span AI system impact assessment, data quality management,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 620.0 Td (human oversight, security, and lifecycle documentation. Opportunities - such as improved model) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 606.0 Td (efficiency or reduced bias - are captured and prioritized alongside risk treatment plans.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 580.0 Td (5. Support: Competence, Awareness, Communication, Documentation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 557.0 Td (HPE ensures the competence of personnel through role-based training in responsible AI, MLOps, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 543.0 Td (model risk, with competency records maintained for data scientists, ML engineers, and reviewers.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 529.0 Td (Awareness programs communicate the AI Policy, individual responsibilities, and the implications of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 515.0 Td (nonconformity to all staff interacting with AI systems. Internal and external communication) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 501.0 Td (protocols define what, when, and to whom AI-related information is disclosed, including) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 487.0 Td (customer-facing model documentation and incident notifications.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 467.0 Td (Documented information required by the AIMS - policies, procedures, risk registers, AIIAs, model) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 453.0 Td (cards, and audit records - is version-controlled, access-restricted, and retained under HPE's) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 439.0 Td (records-management standard.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 413.0 Td (6. AI System Lifecycle and Data Governance) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 390.0 Td (HPE governs the full AI system lifecycle: design, development, verification, validation, deployment,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 376.0 Td (operation, and retirement. Stage-gate reviews at each phase confirm that objectives, controls, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 362.0 Td (impact assessments are satisfied before progression. Human oversight requirements and rollback) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 348.0 Td (procedures are defined for automated decisions in GreenLake AIOps and Aruba AI.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 328.0 Td (Data governance is central to the AIMS. Standards for training data govern quality,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 314.0 Td (representativeness, labeling accuracy, and provenance, ensuring data lineage is traceable from) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 300.0 Td (source to model. Datasets undergo bias and quality screening; provenance metadata records origin,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 286.0 Td (consent basis, and transformation history. HPEFS fraud models apply additional controls for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 272.0 Td (sensitive financial data, and data-retention and minimization rules apply across all three product) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 258.0 Td (lines.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 232.0 Td (7. Performance Evaluation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 209.0 Td (HPE conducts ongoing performance evaluation through continuous monitoring, measurement, and analysis) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 195.0 Td (of AI system behavior against defined objectives and thresholds. Production models are instrumented) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 181.0 Td (for drift, accuracy, fairness, and security metrics, with automated alerts feeding the operations) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 167.0 Td (and governance functions. Scheduled internal audits assess AIMS conformity to ISO/IEC 42001 and the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 153.0 Td (effectiveness of implemented controls, with results reported to top management. Management review is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 139.0 Td (performed at planned intervals to evaluate AIMS suitability, adequacy, and effectiveness,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 125.0 Td (considering audit findings, performance data, and changing risk.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 99.0 Td (8. Improvement) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 76.0 Td (When a nonconformity is identified - through monitoring, audit, incident, or customer feedback - HPE) Tj ET
